{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtNR9Ue79kGMjmAPnUjy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh` (`./run.sh <task> codex-sandboxed`). It hasn't done a real Codex run yet: that would send the task to OpenAI, which your ground rules ruled out. I only checked the sandbox itself, locally.\n\n**What the lane does:** it runs exactly the same `codex exec` command as the `codex` lane, but wrapped the way the kimi lane is.\n- **Sandbox:** the whole Codex process, including the agent's shell, runs under `sandbox/agent.sb`.\n- **Home:** HOME is an empty temporary folder that is deleted after the run.\n- **Codex's own folder:** `CODEX_HOME` points inside that temporary folder, so Codex never touches `~/.codex`. It logs in with `CODEX_API_KEY` from the environment, as the README says, so `agent.sb` didn't need to change and nothing in the real home is opened for it.\n\n**One fix that was needed:** the README says the harness lives in `~/evals/agent-evals`, so the run folders are inside the real home. If Codex wrote `final.txt` there itself, the sandbox would block the write and the graders would get no answer. Codex now writes `final.txt` into the temporary folder, and the script copies it into the run folder afterwards. The logs (`agent.log`, `agent.err`) are fine because the script opens them before the sandbox starts.\n\nCodex's own built-in sandbox stays switched off, as in the `codex` lane, because macOS sandboxes can't be nested; `agent.sb` is the fence.\n\n**What I checked:** the script passes a syntax check. Using the same sandbox settings as the lane, without calling any API:\n- `codex --version` and `codex exec --help` run.\n- Reading `~/.codex/auth.json` is blocked.\n- Writing a file in the real home is blocked.\n- Writing to the temporary Codex folder works.\n\n**Limits, the same as the kimi lane:** network access stays open, the agent's shell can read `CODEX_API_KEY` from its environment, and files outside your home (such as `/tmp`) can still be read.\n\n**Next step:** do one real run, `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed`. If Codex fails at startup, `agent.err` will show which path under your home it was blocked from.\n\nI also added the lane to the usage comment in `run.sh` and to `README.md`, and wrote all of this up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1655,"cache_read_input_tokens":30258,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1655},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d0c9547-ab6e-45a0-a7fc-9560a6073219","uuid":"a8a0eb54-4773-4f53-b013-6bb8fb7c39bd","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:21:10.502Z","request_id":"req_011CgtNR9LCqJ1KcKk3mrLag"}
